{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfvciLoF8nFbKnAkQvjA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fit gives Dq ≈ 1590 cm⁻¹ and B ≈ 780 cm⁻¹ (C = 4.5B ≈ 3510 cm⁻¹).\n\n**Method.** I did not use closed-form band formulas. I built the full d⁶ Hamiltonian numerically and fitted it to the three bands.\n\n1. The basis was all 6-electron Slater determinants with S_z = 0. The Hamiltonian contained the octahedral field (t₂g at −4Dq, e_g at +6Dq) and the electron repulsion written with F₂ = 49B + 7C and F₄ = 63C/5.\n2. I fixed C = 4.5B and diagonalised the Hamiltonian. I kept only the singlet states, using the S² operator to separate them from the triplets, and measured their energies relative to the ¹A₁g ground state.\n3. The spin-allowed bands from ¹A₁g go only to T₁g and T₂g states. I took the three lowest triply degenerate singlet levels, ¹T₁g, ¹T₂g and a higher ¹T₂g/¹T₁g, as the three observed bands.\n4. A least-squares fit of Dq and B to 13 960, 22 740 and 29 700 cm⁻¹ gave Dq = 1591 cm⁻¹ and B = 780 cm⁻¹. Starting the fit from two different guesses gave the same result.\n\n**Calculated bands compared with observed:**\n\n| Band | Observed (cm⁻¹) | Calculated (cm⁻¹) |\n|---|---|---|\n| ¹A₁g → ¹T₁g | 13 960 | 13 936 |\n| ¹A₁g → ¹T₂g | 22 740 | 22 729 |\n| ¹A₁g → third T level | 29 700 | 29 720 |\n\nThe residuals are about 24, 11 and 20 cm⁻¹, so the model reproduces all three bands closely.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1591, \"B\": 780, \"C\": 3510, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Full low-spin d6 ligand-field matrix fit with C/B=4.5 reproduces the three bands to within about 25 cm-1.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2698,"cache_read_input_tokens":6635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2698,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"